> "<exact script the intern reads aloud to the applicant — 2nd person ('you/your'), 2-3 sentences max, plain language, no legal jargon>"

- All scripts and questions addressed to the applicant MUST use 2nd person ("you/your"), never 3rd person ("the applicant").
- If your script says you will ask a question now (for example urgent concurrent checks), you MUST include the exact next question id and wording in the same response. **GEN3-T02 Route D → GEN3-T06** example: `Next: GEN3-T06 Q1 — "Is there an immediate threat to the applicant's (or someone else's) life or physical safety right now?"` (match **`GEN3-T06.json`** Q1 in sources).

